 "request_cards": [],
 "rationale": "Each pair of Toffolis on the same target forms a multiplexer: t ^= s\u00b7u \u2295 (\u00acs)\u00b7v, because the selector s is X-flipped between the two members and the target is never read in between. Each multiplexer equals v \u2295 s\u00b7(u\u2295v), so it needs only one AND. This gives 14 Jones-style 4-T ANDs, computed into one reusable ancilla with measurement uncompute, and the second member of each pair becomes the identity: 56 T on 31 qubits."
